  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsive Local Governance Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  At the local level, people in Bangladesh encounter significant barriers to accessing basic services. The underperformance of local government entities can be attributed to a lack of initiatives or capacity by elected officials, insufficient community demand for accountability, and poor planning and implementing skills. The Responsive Local Governance Activity (RLG) aims to promote decentralization by engaging with all levels of government, enhancing transparent and participatory public administration at the subnational level, and developing local government management capacity through on-the-job training and technical assistance.With FY 2024 funds, RLG will undertake a comprehensive local governance assessment to identify training needs and longer-term reforms, institutionalize best practices, and improve service delivery. The activity will also strengthen connections between local government, the private sector, and both international and local NGOs to improve conditions for marginalized communities. By targeting youth, RLG will engage local government officials on issues critical to this demographic, such as economic advancement and education. By addressing citizen needs at the local level-where local authorities are most accessible-this activity seeks to improve access to basic services and create a platform for the poor, farmers, workers, and women to actively participate in decision-making and development processes.This activity contributes to the Anti-Corruption ($300K) and Youth in Development ($200K). The activity contributes to the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 2.2 - Citizen confidence in governance institutions increases and USAID&apos;s CDCS Mission Development Objective 1 - Democracy strengthened for an inclusive society.</narrative>
  </description>
